{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/pulls/11","id":3718607087,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSV-UXs7dpXDv","html_url":"https://github.com/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/pull/11","diff_url":"https://github.com/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/pull/11.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/pull/11.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/issues/11","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/pulls/11/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/pulls/11/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/issues/11/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Svetozar-Technologies/SatyaVera/statuses/4220684bded0a97b115276e7e4c043904edb10aa","number":11,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Move Next.js API endpoints to Rust","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nFixes #10.\n\nMoves SatyaVera's runtime API surface out of Next.js and into the Rust server workspace. The Next.js app now serves frontend pages only; every `/api/*` endpoint is implemented by `rust/api` and browser fetches are routed through a shared API-base helper.\n\n## What's in this PR\n\n### Rust API server\n\n- Adds `rust/api`, an Axum crate with route parity for the former Next.js API surface:\n  - chat\n  - conversations and messages\n  - documents\n  - guides, templates, dictionary, quizzes\n  - laws and law sections\n  - lawyers and consultations\n  - subscriptions and settings\n  - Razorpay create-order, verify, and webhook endpoints\n- Adds Firebase ID-token verification in Rust, with `SATYAVERA_API_AUTH_DISABLED=1` for local/test runs.\n- Adds process-local rate limiting for high-cost mutating endpoints.\n- Uses the existing Rust transactional journal path when `SATYAVERA_API_JOURNAL_PATH` is set.\n- Loads laws from `SATYAVERA_LAWS_DATA_DIR` and seeds a small built-in catalog for clean checkout tests.\n\n### JavaScript API removal\n\n- Deletes `js/src/app/api/**/route.ts` so Next.js no longer owns runtime API handlers.\n- Removes server-only JavaScript helpers that existed only for those routes:\n  - AI provider/law-search wrappers\n  - API helper/rate-limit utilities\n  - Firebase Admin route helper\n  - Razorpay SDK wrapper\n- Removes unused JS provider/payment packages from `package.json` and `package-lock.json`.\n\n### Frontend API routing\n\n- Adds `js/src/lib/api/client.ts` with `apiUrl()`.\n- Routes browser API calls through `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` or `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE`.\n- Updates CSP `connect-src` to allow the configured Rust API origin and local `http://localhost:8787`.\n- Keeps CI/local builds working without Firebase secrets by using syntactically valid public Firebase fallbacks when env vars are missing or set to the CI placeholder.\n\n### Regression guard and docs\n\n- Adds `npm run check:api-boundary`, which fails if `js/src/app/api` is reintroduced.\n- Runs that guard in `.github/workflows/js.yml`.\n- Updates README, `js/README.md`, `rust/README.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, and `docs/features.md` to describe Rust API ownership and the required env vars.\n- Adds `js/.env.example` with local frontend/Rust API settings.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cd js && npm run check:api-boundary` ✅\n- `cd js && npm run lint` ✅\n- `cd js && npx --yes -p secretlint -p @secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend secretlint \"**/*\" --secretlintignore .gitignore` ✅\n- `cd js && npm run build` ✅\n- `cd js && BASE_PATH=\"/SatyaVera\" NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=\"/SatyaVera\" npm run build:pages` ✅\n- `cd rust && cargo fmt --all -- --check` ✅\n- `cd rust && RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features` ✅\n- `cd rust && RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo test --all-features` ✅\n  - 6 `satyavera-api` route tests\n  - 2 `satyavera-db` unit tests\n  - 3 `satyavera-db` transactional integration tests\n\nNo UI visual changes were made, so no before/after screenshots are included.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- Run the Rust API locally with:\n\n```bash\ncd rust\nSATYAVERA_API_AUTH_DISABLED=1 cargo run -p satyavera-api\n```\n\n- Point the frontend at it with:\n\n```bash\ncd js\nNEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8787 npm run dev\n```\n\n- Production deployments should set `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE` or `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` to the deployed Rust API origin, or provide a same-origin reverse proxy that forwards `/api/*` to Rust.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-05-20T18:10:05Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T13:52:17Z","closed_at":"2026-05-21T13:52:16Z","merged_at":"2026-05-21T13:52:16Z","merge_commit_sha":"17badb41ec88ecc7579f94deff24679d679dde1c","assignee":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard"